screen.LIGHTING=Lighting
screen.WATER=Water
screen.TEXELS=Texel Shading
screen.PERFORMANCE=Performance
option.SUN_BRIGHTNESS=Sun Brightness
option.TORCH_BRIGHTNESS=Torch Brightness
option.EXPOSURE=Exposure
option.FOG_DENSITY=Fog Density
option.WATER_CLARITY=Water Clarity
option.WATER_CLARITY.comment=How far you see into water. Lower is murkier.
option.WATER_SURFACE_OPACITY=Water Surface Opacity
option.WATER_SURFACE_OPACITY.comment=How much of the surface is the water's colour, however shallow.
option.WATER_CAUSTICS_ENABLED=Caustics
option.WATER_CAUSTICS_ENABLED.comment=Rippling light the water's surface casts on the floor below.
value.WATER_CAUSTICS_ENABLED.0=Off
value.WATER_CAUSTICS_ENABLED.1=On
option.WATER_CAUSTICS=Caustics Strength
option.WATER_CAUSTICS.comment=How bright the caustic light is.
option.WATER_CAUSTICS_DEPTH=Caustics Falloff
option.WATER_CAUSTICS_DEPTH.comment=How many blocks deep caustics reach before fading out.
option.WATER_CAUSTICS_SHADE=Caustics in Shadow
option.WATER_CAUSTICS_SHADE.comment=How much shadow on the water dims caustics. 0 keeps them at full strength in shade.
option.WATER_STYLE=Water Style
option.WATER_STYLE.comment=Waves ripple the surface. Flat keeps it still and glints on the texture, and costs less. Immersive is flat, coloured by the texture, clouds with depth and mirrors at grazing angles.
value.WATER_STYLE.0=Waves
value.WATER_STYLE.1=Flat
value.WATER_STYLE.2=Immersive
option.GOD_RAY_STEPS=God Ray Steps
option.WATER_REFLECTIONS=Water Reflections
option.WATER_REFLECTIONS.comment=Water mirrors the world and the sky.
option.REFLECTION_QUALITY=Reflection Quality
option.REFLECTION_QUALITY.comment=Higher quality finds finer detail and costs more performance.
value.REFLECTION_QUALITY.0=Low
value.REFLECTION_QUALITY.1=Normal
value.REFLECTION_QUALITY.2=High
option.REFLECTION_STRENGTH=Reflection Strength
option.REFLECTION_STRENGTH.comment=How strong reflections are.
option.WATER_COLOR_MAPPING=Water Color Mapping
option.WATER_COLOR_MAPPING.comment=Immersive water: colour follows the biome and fades with depth. Off keeps the vanilla texture.
option.GLINT_SMOOTHNESS=Glint Smoothness
option.GLINT_SMOOTHNESS.comment=0% gives sharp sparkling pixels. 100% gives a soft, gentle sheen.
option.SHADOW_SOFTNESS=Shadow Softness
option.VOLUMETRIC_RES=Light Shaft Resolution
option.VOLUMETRIC_RES.comment=The fraction of the screen fog and light shafts are marched at.
value.VOLUMETRIC_RES.1=Full
value.VOLUMETRIC_RES.2=1/2
value.VOLUMETRIC_RES.3=1/3
value.VOLUMETRIC_RES.4=1/4
option.SCALED_RESOLVE=Scaled Effects
option.SCALED_RESOLVE.comment=How reduced-resolution effects return to full resolution: a smooth, edge-aware upsample, or a crisp ordered dither.
value.SCALED_RESOLVE.0=Upsample
value.SCALED_RESOLVE.1=Dither
option.TEXEL_FULL_DISTANCE=Full Texel Distance
option.TEXEL_FULL_DISTANCE.comment=Blocks from you that shade at full detail, 16 texels per block. Past it, shading gets coarser in rings.
option.TEXEL_RING_WIDTH=Texel Ring Width
option.TEXEL_RING_WIDTH.comment=How many blocks wide each coarser ring is. Each ring halves the texels per block.
option.TEXEL_MIN_RES=Minimum Texels
option.TEXEL_MIN_RES.comment=The fewest texels per block far surfaces shade at.
option.TEXEL_DENOISE=Texel Denoise
option.TEXEL_DENOISE.comment=How many points across each coarse texel its shadow averages. More is steadier under leaves and plants, at more shadow lookups far away. 1 is off.
option.TEXEL_DENOISE_RES=Denoise Threshold
option.TEXEL_DENOISE_RES.comment=Texels this coarse or coarser are denoised, in texels per block. Finer texels shade at a single point, in real time.
option.TEXEL_TEMPORAL=Temporal Denoise
option.TEXEL_TEMPORAL.comment=Frames of history the coarsest texels' shadows average over, with new points scattered across the texel every frame; finer texels keep less (half per step), so they follow moving shadows more closely. Steadier under swaying plants and kelp, with a slight trail on fast shadows. 0 is off.
option.TEXEL_TEMPORAL_POINTS=Temporal Points
option.TEXEL_TEMPORAL_POINTS.comment=Points each denoised texel takes a frame while the history averages them. More converges faster, at more shadow lookups.
option.shadowMapResolution=Shadow Resolution
option.shadowMapResolution.comment=Texels across the shadow map. Lower is faster on weak GPUs, with softer, blockier shadows.
option.shadowDistance=Shadow Distance
option.shadowDistance.comment=Blocks from you that cast shadows. Shorter is faster and sharper up close.
option.FOLIAGE_SHADING=Foliage Shading
option.FOLIAGE_SHADING.comment=How plants like grass, flowers and sugar cane are shadowed. Fancy: texels on the plant, like the blocks around it. Fast: one lookup per corner, softer. Potato: one shade per plant block, nearly free.
value.FOLIAGE_SHADING.0=Fancy
value.FOLIAGE_SHADING.1=Fast
value.FOLIAGE_SHADING.2=Potato
option.torchShadowCache=Shadow Caching
option.torchShadowCache.comment=Keep the terrain shadow map between frames and redraw it only when the sun steps, you move 8 blocks, or terrain in it changes. Off redraws every frame.
value.torchShadowCache.true=On
value.torchShadowCache.false=Off (Real Time)
option.torchShadowStep=Sun Step
option.torchShadowStep.comment=Degrees the sun moves between cached shadow redraws. Smaller is smoother and slower.
option.torchShadowLerp=Sun Step Blending
option.torchShadowLerp.comment=Fade from the last step's shadows to the new ones over each step. Costs a second shadow lookup.
value.torchShadowLerp.true=On
value.torchShadowLerp.false=Off
screen.CLOUDS=Clouds
option.CLOUD_STYLE=Cloud Style
option.CLOUD_STYLE.comment=Soft lights clouds by the sky around them and melts them into it far off. Classic lights them as a plain surface.
value.CLOUD_STYLE.0=Soft
value.CLOUD_STYLE.1=Classic
option.CLOUD_BLEND_DISTANCE=Cloud Sky Blend
option.CLOUD_BLEND_DISTANCE.comment=Blocks out by which clouds have melted into the sky.
option.CLOUD_SCATTER=Cloud Sun Glow
option.CLOUD_SCATTER.comment=How brightly clouds glow looking toward the sun.
option.torchCloudUpper=Upper Cloud Layer
option.torchCloudUpper.comment=A second, thinner cloud layer 30 blocks above the first, with its own pattern.
value.torchCloudUpper.true=On
value.torchCloudUpper.false=Off
